=== stdout ===
OVERVIEW: Firebase Crashlytics from the terminal, with clean JSON for
developers and AI agents.

USAGE: xcrashlytics <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  init                    Write .xcrashlytics.json in the current directory and
                          verify the Firebase setup.
  use                     Switch the active Firebase app profile.
  issues                  List Firebase Crashlytics issues.
  events                  List Firebase Crashlytics events for one or more
                          issues.
  show                    Show a single crash by id (XC-<uuid>, FB-<id>) or
                          Firebase console link.
  export                  Export one crash as a shareable report: what it is,
                          how much it hurts, where it happens.
  open                    Open a crash's source location in Xcode via xed.
  blame                   Aggregate top blamed Firebase frames.
  groups                  Show related Firebase issues and optional Xcode
                          crashes.
  breakdown               Exact events and users per app version, OS version,
                          or device model — for one issue or the whole app.

  See 'xcrashlytics help <subcommand>' for detailed help.
